6952#issuecomment-500170142","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/6952","id":500170142,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUwMDE3MDE0Mg==","user":{"login":"Michael0x2a","id":1424628,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MjQ2Mjg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1424628?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Michael0x2a","html_url":"https://github.com/Michael0x2a","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Michael0x2a/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Michael0x2a/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Michael0x2a/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Michael0x2a/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Michael0x2a/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Michael0x2a/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Michael0x2a/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Michael0x2a/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Michael0x2a/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-06-08T22:27:40Z","updated_at":"2019-06-08T22:44:43Z","body":"~This seems to be related to how we handle the type context in some way.~\r\n\r\n~Mypy seems to correctly remember that the type of `var` has a `last_known_value` of 42 in each iteration of the new semantic analyzer, but the type context seems to contain just Nones in the final iteration. So, `var` is treated as just an `int` at that stage, which is why we get the type error.~\r\n\r\n~(It's a bit puzzling though -- I don't see why the behavior of the new semantic analyzer would influence the type checking phase in this way?)~\r\n\r\n~I'll try digging a bit deeper.~","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/500170142/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"roc